menu "Kit loopback"

    config KIT_MIC_GAIN
        int "Mic gain (linear multiplier)"
        range 1 64
        default 8
        help
            The INMP441 is fairly quiet. Samples are multiplied by this
            before being sent to the DACs. 8 is a sane default for speech.

    config KIT_AMP_ALWAYS_ON
        bool "Keep the speaker amp on all the time"
        default n
        help
            By default the MAX98357A is only enabled while the encoder button
            is held (push-to-talk), because mic -> speaker loopback howls when
            the speaker is near the mic. Enable this if you have no encoder
            wired yet or want to test the speaker freely.

    config KIT_SAMPLE_RATE
        int "Sample rate (Hz)"
        default 16000
        help
            Shared by mic and both DACs (they share BCLK/WS). 16000 or 48000
            are good choices. All three chips accept both.

endmenu
